travenous leiomyomatosis of the uterus. A clinicopathologic study of 22 cases</article-title><source>Int J Gynecol Pathol</source><year>1994</year><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>9</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8112951</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Evans</surname><given-names>ATI</given-names></name><name><surname>Symmonds</surname><given-names>RE</given-names></name><name><surname>Gaffey</surname><given-names>TA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Recurrent pelvic intravenous leiomyomatosis</article-title><source>Obstet Gynecol</source><year>1981</year><fpage>260</fpage><lpage>64</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7465135</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>